  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that RNA-only multiprofile avgpool with scvi_n200 is best (accuracy 0.650, F1 0.628), and multiprofile avgpool also improved PCA over singleprofile. The key uncertainty is whether the scvi improvement is due to the learned encoder itself or to multiprofile averaging. config_004 tests scvi_n200 in the simpler singleprofile setting, isolating the profile-setting effect for the best RNA encoder. This is a single-factor extension of the most promising direction, has high expected utility, and clarifies whether a simpler RNA-only model may be sufficient before adding image modalities or more complex aggregation."
